    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Strong Q3 and higher guidance, but share sales and an AI selloff knock DOCN down",
               "technical":  "The trend is clearly down. On 20 November DOCN closed at USD 66.76, down 13.4%. It opened at 73.90 and finished near the day\u0027s low of 65.55. Price sits far below all three EMAs (exponential moving averages that weight recent prices more): EMA50 at 100.80, EMA100 at 109.73 and EMA200 at 105.04. The EMA50 has fallen below both longer averages, the usual order in a downtrend. MACD (the gap between a fast and a slow average, used to read momentum) is deeply negative at -9.12. It is only just above its signal line at -9.16, so the histogram is a barely positive +0.04. That hints the selling is slowing but is not yet a turn. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 31.04, right at the edge of oversold. Price is just above the lower Bollinger Band at 64.10 (bands drawn two standard deviations around the 20-day average). The bands are very wide (64.10 to 107.13), which shows how violent the swings have been. The stock sits about 17% of the way up its 52-week range of 42.01–187.50. Volume of 5.47M was about 1.35x the 20-day average, so the sell-off had real participation. The lower band near 64 is the first support. The 20-day average near 85.6 is the first resistance.",
               "fundamental":  "The business got stronger this quarter. On 3 November DigitalOcean reported Q3 revenue of USD 321M, up 40% year on year and above its own 304–307M guidance. Adjusted EPS was 0.45. Revenue from AI customers, counted as annual recurring revenue (ARR), rose 288% to USD 376M. About 90% of it now comes from managed inference and platform services rather than bare GPU rental. That supports the developer-experience thesis. Guidance went up: Q4 revenue of 348–351M (+44–45%), full-year 2026 of 1,208–1,211M, and 2027 growth of 60% or more (previously 50% or more). The catch is capital. The company is building about 180 MW of committed data-centre capacity, using a USD 785M equipment lease, and on 2 November it signed a program to sell up to USD 1B of new shares at market prices. That is roughly 11% dilution at current prices, plus earlier share issuance to retire convertible notes.",
               "news":  [
                            "3 Nov 2026: Q3 revenue was USD 321M (+40%), with record incremental ARR of USD 160M. Management raised Q4 guidance to +44–45% growth and the 2027 outlook to +60% or more.",
                            "2–3 Nov 2026: DigitalOcean set up a program with Goldman Sachs and other banks to sell up to USD 1B of common stock \u0027at the market\u0027, meaning gradually at prevailing prices. That raised dilution worries even as results beat.",
                            "4 Nov 2026: Shares fell about 3.7% intraday after Datadog\u0027s cautious Q4 guidance raised concerns about cloud usage. Goldman Sachs cut its target to USD 156 from 178 and kept a Buy rating. At least six firms lowered their targets.",
                            "Week ended 6 Nov 2026: DOCN fell 19% to USD 72.48, including a 15.85% drop on 5 Nov. That day the Nasdaq fell 5.5% as investors sold AI infrastructure stocks after the US midterm elections.",
                            "20 Nov 2026: A broad AI sell-off tied to a fading Anthropic IPO, Nvidia\u0027s 13.8% fall and expectations of a December Fed rate hike pushed the S\u0026P 500 into a correction. Neocloud peers CoreWeave (-12.1%) and Nebius (-16.1%) fell alongside DOCN\u0027s 13.4% drop. Reports found no DigitalOcean-specific news that day."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The recent damage comes from financing and market sentiment, not weak operations. Those drivers can last longer than expected. The USD 1B share sale means new shares could be sold into any rally, which may cap rebounds. Growing toward 150 MW of capacity by 2027 makes DigitalOcean more capital-intensive and closer to the debt-funded neocloud model the market is now punishing. Even after the fall, GuruFocus put the trailing P/E near 287x. A December rate hike or a deeper AI-capex pullback could push the stock toward the 52-week low of USD 42.01.",
               "opportunity":  "Price has fallen hard while the numbers improved. This is DigitalOcean\u0027s fifth straight quarter of faster growth, and guidance was raised on 3 November. RSI near 31, price at the lower Bollinger Band and a MACD histogram turning slightly positive suggest selling pressure may be nearing exhaustion, though none of this confirms a bottom. If the market stabilises, a move back toward the 20-day average near USD 85.6 would be an ordinary bounce. The shift toward higher-value inference services is the part that matters for long-term holders.",
               "risks":  [
                             "Dilution from the USD 1B share sale and earlier share issuance to retire convertible notes",
                             "Sector-wide de-rating of neocloud and AI infrastructure stocks as investors question debt-funded capex",
                             "Higher interest rates (a December Fed hike is priced in) hurting richly valued growth stocks",
                             "Delays or cost overruns on the roughly 180 MW of committed data-centre capacity",
                             "Competition from hyperscalers and GPU neoclouds eroding the simplicity advantage for small and mid-sized customers"
                         ],
               "summary":  "DOCN is in a steep downtrend. At USD 66.76 it sits far below all three EMAs and just above the lower Bollinger Band, with RSI near oversold at 31. The fundamentals point the other way: Q3 revenue grew 40%, AI ARR almost quadrupled, and 2027 guidance rose to 60% or more growth. The drop comes from a USD 1B share-sale program and two AI-sector selloffs (5 and 20 November), not from operating weakness. The moat thesis is intact. Dilution and financing costs are the issues to track, with Q4 results in February the next checkpoint."
           },
    "th":  {
               "headline":  "งบ Q3 แข็งแรงและเพิ่มเป้า แต่แผนขายหุ้นใหม่กับกระแสเทขายหุ้น AI กดราคา DOCN",
               "technical":  "แนวโน้มเป็นขาลงชัดเจน วันที่ 20 พ.ย. DOCN ปิดที่ 66.76 ดอลลาร์ ลดลง 13.4% โดยเปิดที่ 73.90 แล้วปิดใกล้จุดต่ำสุดของวันที่ 65.55 ราคาอยู่ต่ำกว่า EMA (เส้นค่าเฉลี่ยที่ให้น้ำหนักราคาล่าสุดมากกว่า) ทั้งสามเส้นอย่างห่างไกล คือ EMA50 ที่ 100.80, EMA100 ที่ 109.73 และ EMA200 ที่ 105.04 EMA50 หลุดลงไปอยู่ใต้เส้นระยะยาวทั้งสองเส้นแล้ว ซึ่งเป็นการเรียงตัวแบบขาลง MACD (ส่วนต่างระหว่างค่าเฉลี่ยเร็วกับช้า ใช้ดูโมเมนตัม) ติดลบลึกที่ -9.12 และอยู่เหนือเส้นสัญญาณที่ -9.16 เพียงนิดเดียว histogram จึงบวกแค่ +0.04 บอกได้ว่าแรงขายเริ่มชะลอ แต่ยังไม่ใช่การกลับตัว RSI 14 (มาตรวัดโมเมนตัม 0–100 ต่ำกว่า 30 ถือว่าขายมากเกินไป) อยู่ที่ 31.04 เกือบถึงโซน oversold ราคาอยู่เหนือขอบล่างของ Bollinger Band ที่ 64.10 เพียงเล็กน้อย (กรอบ 2 ส่วนเบี่ยงเบนมาตรฐานรอบค่าเฉลี่ย 20 วัน) กรอบกว้างมากตั้งแต่ 64.10 ถึง 107.13 สะท้อนความผันผวนที่รุนแรง ราคาอยู่ราว 17% ของกรอบ 52 สัปดาห์ (42.01–187.50) วอลุ่ม 5.47 ล้านหุ้น สูงกว่าค่าเฉลี่ย 20 วันราว 1.35 เท่า แปลว่าการขายมีแรงหนุนจริง แนวรับแรกคือขอบล่างแถว 64 แนวต้านแรกคือค่าเฉลี่ย 20 วันแถว 85.6",
